## Findings

- **Medium — Task metadata migration path is still unreachable**  
  The PR comments are correct: `migrateOneCheckpoint` gates task metadata copy on `info.IsTask && info.ToolUseID != ""`, but `info` comes from `ListCommitted`, which currently does not populate those fields. That means `copyTaskMetadataToV2` won’t run for task checkpoints.

```181:189:cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go
// Copy task metadata trees from v1 to v2 /full/current
if info.IsTask && info.ToolUseID != "" {
	if taskErr := copyTaskMetadataToV2(ctx, repo, v1Store, v2Store, info.CheckpointID, summary); taskErr != nil {
		logging.Warn(ctx, "failed to copy task metadata to v2",
			slog.String("checkpoint_id", string(info.CheckpointID)),
			slog.String("error", taskErr.Error()),
		)
	}
}
```

```903:927:cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go
info := CommittedInfo{
	CheckpointID: checkpointID,
}
// ...
if json.Unmarshal([]byte(sessionContent), &sessionMetadata) == nil {
	info.Agent = sessionMetadata.Agent
	info.SessionID = sessionMetadata.SessionID
	info.CreatedAt = sessionMetadata.CreatedAt
}
```

- **Medium — Prompt delimiter handling is still incorrect and can corrupt prompt boundaries**  
  `buildMigrateWriteOpts` splits `content.Prompts` by `"\n"`, but v1/v2 persisted prompt separators are `"\n\n---\n\n"`. Multi-line prompts and multi-prompt checkpoints can be reconstructed incorrectly.

```203:210:cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go
var prompts []string
if content.Prompts != "" {
	prompts = strings.Split(content.Prompts, "\n")
	// Remove trailing empty string from trailing newline
	if len(prompts) > 0 && prompts[len(prompts)-1] == "" {
		prompts = prompts[:len(prompts)-1]
	}
}
```

- **Low — Test coverage comment is valid; task-metadata assertion is missing**  
  The current task migration test only checks summary presence in v2 and does not assert `tasks/` tree splice outcome in `/full/current`, so regressions in `copyTaskMetadataToV2` can slip through.

```217:221:cmd/entire/cli/migrate_test.go
// Verify task checkpoint exists in v2
summary, readErr := v2Store.ReadCommitted(context.Background(), cpID)
require.NoError(t, readErr)
require.NotNil(t, summary)
```

## Open question / nuance

- Copilot’s suggested `TrimSpace` when splitting prompts is likely too aggressive for fidelity: it can alter leading/trailing whitespace that may be meaningful in prompts. Better to split on the true separator and preserve prompt text exactly (except maybe removing a final empty segment if the stored format guarantees one).

## Verdict on the PR comments

- The two Bugbot comments and Copilot’s test-coverage comment on [PR #855](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/855) are all valid against the current branch state.
